< {"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":2,"result":{"tools":[{"name":"status","title":"Renoise status","description":"Whether Kumi's bridge in Renoise is connected: the Renoise and bridge versions, the open project, and whether Renoise is busy (a dialog, a render). With several Renoise instances running, pass pid or resource from discover.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"pid":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"description":"The Renoise process to use, from discover, when several run."},"resource":{"type":"string","description":"The Renoise resource or preferences folder to use, from discover, when several run."}},"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":true,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false}},{"name":"discover","title":"Find running Renoise","description":"Every running Renoise with Kumi's bridge: process id, port, resource folder, versions, open project, and whether it answers. Use it when status reports none, or to choose among several.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{},"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":true,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false}},{"name":"read","title":"Read Renoise","description":"Rows of one kind from the open Renoise project, a page at a time: {items, nextCursor?, epoch}. Pass parent (a row's ref) to read what is inside it, such as a track's items or an FX's parameters; pass the previous page's nextCursor as cursor for the next page. Or pass ref alone for the one object it names. Refs hold until the epoch changes. With several Renoise instances running, pass pid or resource from discover.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"pid":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"description":"The Renoise process to use, from discover, when several run."},"resource":{"type":"string","description":"The Renoise resource or preferences folder to use, from discover, when several run."},"kind":{"type":"string","enum":["song","track","sequence","pattern","line","instrument","sample","phrase","device","param","modset","chain"],"description":"What to read in Renoise."},"parent":{"type":"string","description":"The ref of what the rows are in: a track for its items or sends, an FX for its parameters."},"ref":{"type":"string","description":"The ref of one object to read instead of a page of rows."},"cursor":{"type":"string","description":"The nextCursor an earlier page gave, unchanged."},"limit":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"maximum":200,"description":"Rows in a page (50 by default)."},"track":{"type":["integer","string"],"description":"For kind line: the track (its number, or its ref) whose lines of the parent pattern to read."},"layout":{"type":"integer","minimum":0,"description":"The layout the refs were read in (each answer and tracks event says it): refs from an older one are carried through the track shifts since."},"hidden":{"type":"boolean","description":"Also list data in the note and effect columns the track doesn't show, on every line (under `hidden`). Without it only a line with nothing in the shown columns is looked through."}},"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":true,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false}},{"name":"snapshot","title":"Renoise snapshot","description":"The open Renoise project on one screen: {epoch, project, transport, tracks, selection, markers?}. What is too big to include is named under truncated, to read with `read`.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"pid":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"description":"The Renoise process to use, from discover, when several run."},"resource":{"type":"string","description":"The Renoise resource or preferences folder to use, from discover, when several run."}},"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":true,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false}},{"name":"focus","title":"Renoise focus","description":"What the producer is looking at in Renoise: {epoch, view, selection, transport, changed}. Cheap enough to poll about every 150 ms; read again only when changed moves.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"pid":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"description":"The Renoise process to use, from discover, when several run."},"resource":{"type":"string","description":"The Renoise resource or preferences folder to use, from discover, when several run."}},"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":true,"idempotentHint":false,"openWorldHint":false}},{"name":"focus_body","title":"Renoise view","description":"What Renoise shows in one of its views, ready to draw: pass kind, and ref (the take, track or pattern it is about) or window (the range to show) where the kind takes them. Long ones come in pages: pass the nextCursor as cursor.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"pid":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"description":"The Renoise process to use, from discover, when several run."},"resource":{"type":"string","description":"The Renoise resource or preferences folder to use, from discover, when several run."},"kind":{"type":"string","enum":["pattern","matrix","phrase","instrument","dsp"],"description":"Which view."},"ref":{"type":"string","description":"The ref of what the view is about."},"around":{"type":"string","description":"The ref of a track to centre the first page of tracks on (the arrange view): the page starts half a page above it, and says where in `from`."},"window":{"type":"object","properties":{"from":{"type":"number"},"to":{"type":"number"}},"required":["from","to"],"additionalProperties":false,"description":"The range to show, in the view's own units."},"cursor":{"type":"string","description":"The nextCursor an earlier page gave, unchanged."},"limit":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"maximum":200,"description":"Rows in a page."},"layout":{"type":"integer","minimum":0,"description":"The layout the refs were read in (each answer and tracks event says it): refs from an older one are carried through the track shifts since."},"hidden":{"type":"boolean","description":"Also list data in the note and effect columns the track doesn't show, on every line (under `hidden`). Without it only a line with nothing in the shown columns is looked through."}},"required":["kind"],"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":true,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false}},{"name":"change_preview","title":"Preview a Renoise change","description":"What one change would do in Renoise, without making it: {transactionId, confirmation, prior, display, target, epoch}. Apply it with change_apply.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"pid":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"description":"The Renoise process to use, from discover, when several run."},"resource":{"type":"string","description":"The Renoise resource or preferences folder to use, from discover, when several run."},"kind":{"type":"string","description":"The change kind."},"input":{"type":"object","description":"What the kind takes."},"epoch":{"type":"string","description":"The epoch the refs in input came from."},"layout":{"type":"integer","minimum":0,"description":"The layout the refs were read in (each answer and tracks event says it): refs from an older one are carried through the track shifts since."}},"required":["kind","input"],"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":true,"idempotentHint":false,"openWorldHint":false}},{"name":"change_apply","title":"Apply a Renoise change","description":"Makes a previewed change in Renoise, as one named step of Renoise's undo. The same idempotencyKey again returns the first answer and changes nothing. state is applied, or uncertain when Renoise didn't answer.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"transactionId":{"type":"string"},"confirmation":{"type":"string","description":"The confirmation change_preview gave."},"idempotencyKey":{"type":"string"},"title":{"type":"string","description":"The change's name in Renoise's undo history."}},"required":["transactionId","confirmation","idempotencyKey"],"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":false,"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false}},{"name":"change_undo","title":"Undo a Renoise change","description":"Takes a change back as a new named step in Renoise: exactly what it changed is put back. Refused (code changed) if those values changed since, unless discard.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"transactionId":{"type":"string"},"confirmation":{"const":"undo"},"idempotencyKey":{"type":"string"},"discard":{"type":"boolean","description":"Put the values back even if they changed since."}},"required":["transactionId","confirmation","idempotencyKey"],"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":false,"destructiveHint":true,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false}},{"name":"transport_stop","title":"Stop Renoise","description":"Stops Renoise's playback and recording at once.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"pid":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"description":"The Renoise process to use, from discover, when several run."},"resource":{"type":"string","description":"The Renoise resource or preferences folder to use, from discover, when several run."}},"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":false,"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false}},{"name":"transport_play","title":"Play Renoise","description":"Starts Renoise's playback from where it is, or (Renoise) from sequence (a slot, from 1) and line.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"pid":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"description":"The Renoise process to use, from discover, when several run."},"resource":{"type":"string","description":"The Renoise resource or preferences folder to use, from discover, when several run."},"sequence":{"type":"integer","minimum":1},"line":{"type":"integer","minimum":1},"epoch":{"type":"string"}},"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":false,"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false}},{"name":"cursor_set","title":"Move Renoise's cursor","description":"Moves Renoise's edit cursor to positionBeats (quarter notes from the start) or position (seconds); the play position follows while it plays.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"pid":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"description":"The Renoise process to use, from discover, when several run."},"resource":{"type":"string","description":"The Renoise resource or preferences folder to use, from discover, when several run."},"positionBeats":{"type":"number","minimum":0},"position":{"type":"number","minimum":0},"epoch":{"type":"string"}},"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":false,"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false}},{"name":"undo_step_begin","title":"Begin one Renoise undo step","description":"Opens one step of Renoise's undo around the changes that follow, where Renoise gives one: {stepId}. Close it with undo_step_end.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"label":{"type":"string"}},"required":["label"],"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":false,"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":false,"openWorldHint":false}},{"name":"undo_step_end","title":"End the Renoise undo step","description":"Closes the step undo_step_begin opened; label names it in Renoise's undo by what it did.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"stepId":{"type":"string"},"label":{"type":"string","maxLength":200}},"required":["stepId"],"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":false,"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false}},{"name":"change_release","title":"Forget changes","description":"Changes that won't be undone any more: the host forgets them (at most 64 at a time).","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"transactionIds":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"},"minItems":1,"maxItems":64}},"required":["transactionIds"],"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":false,"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false}},{"name":"project_save","title":"Save the Renoise song","description":"Saves the open Renoise song where it is. A song never saved is saved only under path, and never over a file. (version is REAPER's: Renoise refuses it.)","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"pid":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"description":"The Renoise process to use, from discover, when several run."},"resource":{"type":"string","description":"The Renoise resource or preferences folder to use, from discover, when several run."},"version":{"type":"boolean"},"path":{"type":"string"},"epoch":{"type":"string","description":"The epoch of the answer the project was read in: if the project open now is another, the save is refused as stale."}},"required":["epoch"],"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":false,"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false}},{"name":"instrument_save","title":"Save a Renoise instrument","description":"Saves an instrument to an .xrni file at path (absolute; the extension is added when missing), never over a file already there unless overwrite: true. Not a change: no undo.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"pid":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"description":"The Renoise process to use, from discover, when several run."},"resource":{"type":"string","description":"The Renoise resource or preferences folder to use, from discover, when several run."},"instrumentRef":{"type":"string","description":"The instrument."},"ref":{"type":"string","description":"The instrument (as instrumentRef)."},"path":{"type":"string"},"overwrite":{"type":"boolean"},"epoch":{"type":"string"},"layout":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"required":["path"],"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":false,"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false}}]}}
